Please help me to find the title of a book!
A few years ago I remember reading a crime / thriller and I can still remember almost the entire plot, however, the title partout doesn’t want to occur to me anymore maybe someone knows here...
The story was about fear and treating it.
At the beginning of the story, an animal keeper commits suicide by showering himself with fodder and walks into the enclosure for his predatory cats.
The case is taken over by a commissioner who, after a short investigation to his therapist, runs a clinic where he treats anxiety patients.
The commissioner has a small niece who is also afraid (of fire) and ends up with this therapist.
There is more suicide and there is another protagonist - a photographer who is commissioned anonymously before every suicide to go and document the location of self-murder and put the photos on the internet.
In any case, it ultimately turns out that this therapist operates a kind of underground therapy group where the patient is transplanted a chip who suppresses an anxiety center in the brain and the patients ultimately face their fear in the most extreme way.
(a woman jumps out ofrom the window another deliberately drives herself to death)
This face of fear is referred to as "the fight" in the book.
In the end, there's a big showdund in the clinic that had to do with a fire.
This is so the rough plot I am quite sure that the book was written in the original by a French author.
If this plot is known to someone or even someone can tell me the title of the book I would be very happy.
