All Bosch power tools, compressed air tools and measuring tools are carefully inspected, tested and are subject to the strict controls of Bosch quality assurance.
Bosch therefore provides a guarantee for Bosch power tools, compressed air tools and measuring tools.
The Buyer’s claims for liability for defects from the purchase contract with the Seller as well as legal rights will not be restricted by this guarantee.
For these tools we provide warranty according to the following conditions:
In accordance with the following regulations (No. 2 – 7), we provide a guarantee by free correction of the deficiencies in the tools, which are proven to be based on a material or manufacturing defect within the warranty period.
The warranty period is 24 months, in the case of commercial or professional use or equalivatory use 12 months.
The warranty period begins with the purchase by the first-end customer.
The date is decisive on the original purchase document.
For all commercial, blue power tools and measuring tools purchased from 01.09.2004 (with the exception of high-frequency tools, industrial battery screwdrivers and compressed air tools), the warranty period is extended to 36 months if the buyer registers these tools within 4 weeks from the date of purchase.
Battery packs and chargers as well as included accessories are excluded from this warranty extension.
Registration can only be carried out on the Internet at www.bosch-pt.com/warranty
Confirmation is the registration document, which must be printed out immediately, as well as the original purchase receipt from which the date of the purchase emerges.
Registration is only possible if the buyer agrees to the storage of his data entered there.
Excluded from the warranty are: parts that are subject to use-related or other natural wear and tear, as well as deficiencies in the tool, which are due to use-related or other natural use, abnormal environmental conditions, non-substantive operating conditions, overload or lack of maintenance or care.
Deficiencies in the tool caused by the use of accessories, supplements or spare parts that are not Bosch original parts.
tools on which modifications or additions have been made.
Minor deviations from the desired quality, which are insignificant for the value and usability of the tool.
The remedy of the defect recognized by us as obligated to guarantee takes place in such a way that we repair the defective tool free of charge at our option or replace it with a flawless tool (possibly also a successor model).
Replaced tools or parts are transferred to our property.
