LokSound 5 is the most important member of the LokSound family.
Thanks to the combination of digital decoder and sound module on a printed circuit board, we achieve dimensions of only 30mm x15.5mm and can thus be installed in almost any locomotive of the H0 and 0 gauges.
LokSound 5 decoders are offered with all common interfaces and always come with an 11x15mm “sugar cube” loudspeaker together with sound capsule kit.
Like all family members, the LokSound5 is a true multi-protocol decoder.
He masters the DCC data format as well as Motorola®, Selectrix® and M4.
In DCC format, 14 to 128 driving levels are as natural as 2- and 4-digit addresses and up to 32 functions.
Thanks to RailComPlus®, the decoders register fully automatically at a suitable digital center.
He masters all DCC programming modes and thanks to RailCom® the CV values can be readed on the main track with suitable controls.
There are auxiliary registers for control panels that only programme the CVs of 1-255.
Motorola® users benefit from up to 28 levels at 255 addresses.
Three more Motorola® addresses allow the triggering of 16 functions.
A built-in programming mode also makes reprogramming possible with the venerable Control Unit 6021.
The M4 protocol allows automatic login to mfx®-compatible controls.
The LokSound 5 decoder recognizes the Märklin® braking distances as well as ZIMO® HLU brake commands or the Lenz® ABC system.
It is also possible to brake with DCC brake modules or with direct voltage.
In addition, it also lasts with a Selectrix® brake diode.
An ABC commuter train automatic allows automatic commuting between two stations.
The LokSound 5 decoder can be used on analogue direct and alternating current paths.
