Content warning: I’m going to write a bit in detail about domestic violence here.
I've just got to write something about my soul.
For professional reasons, I (21) are more likely to come into contact with victims (and perpetrators) of domestic violence.
A topic that really gnaws at me and unfortunately seems far too common is that many victims do not allow themselves to be helped or think we could not help them.
It is quite clear to me that we cannot do everything and it is not perfect.
But there are fewer things in my profession that move me more than when I can't do anything in such situations.
I see the bruises, the blood, the desperate eyes...
But even in conversation in private, with the perpetrator far out of sight and hearing, I can't reach everyone.
I don't know what's the reason, maybe it's afraid, afraid of revenge, fear of leaving the usual social environment, afraid of snatching the children out of it.
What I always want to make it clear to everyone is sometimes very close to the tears themselves, everyone is worthy to be able to live without violence.
I want all women to know that they don't just have to accept violence.
Often I wish I could help with this in any case... I know I can't do it.
But it will never be easier.
Please, always remember, you are worth living without violence, that's so unbelievably important.
