Basketball-Bundesliga: Derby debacle of the MHP giants Ludwigsburg at the Merlins Crailsheim
At least youngster Johannes Patrick was relied upon.
Again nothing: For the second time in less than three months, the giants lost in Crailsheim - and how!
Before the game, Ludwigsburg's coach John Patrick had said with a review of the cup defeat in early October at the Hakro Merlins Crailsheim: "We still have some anger in our stomachs".
After the game, however, it did not settle - but increased again in view of the 61:72 (28:38) defeat in the basketball league.
Even more than the naked result disappointed the manner of the performance.
Representative is a statistic that expresses the entire dilemma: The three-way quota was only 13 percent, 4 hits (all from the young Johannes Patrick) with 31 attempts - still questions?
John Patrick said: “We just weren’t focused enough after the win at Tenerife and didn’t implement what we coached.”
Namely moving the ball.
Quite another, his counterpart Sebastian Gleim reacted: "To win a horny game for the second time against Ludwigsburg," said the happy coach.
"It felt like 10 000 people."
Only 750 visitors were allowed in the Hohenlohe Arena on Saturday, but they got their money's worth.
Not least because of BBL top scorer T.J. Shorts, who marked 22 points and steered his team's game.
"The best playmaker I've ever coached," Gleim said.
While in Patrick's team himself the top performers such as Jordan Hulls (0 points) and Jonah Radebaugh (7) failed across the line.
Only in the last quarter (22:15) the giants prevented a total debacle and came up to eight points, after they had already been 39:59 behind.
In addition to Johannes Patrick, Justin Simon scored twelve points.
Fortunately, there is not much time to quarrel.
Already on Wednesday (19 o'clock) the giants receive the Skyliners Frankfurt, before then also in Ludwigsburg a maximum of 750 spectators.
