Federal Building Minister Klara Geywitz: Expropriation does not create a new apartment
The new Federal Minister of Construction Klara Geywitz (SPD) has spoken out against the expropriation of large housing corporations, as has been demanded in Berlin in a referendum.
"With an expropriation, not a single new apartment emerges, only the ownership structure changes," Geywitz said in an interview with "Tagesspiegel" (Sunday).
My goal is to give tenants certainty that their rent will remain affordable over the next few years.
By the way, a colorful mix of, for example, private landlords, cooperatives or housing associations is the best protection against monopoly formation.
In Berlin, the coalition of the SPD, the Greens and the Left Party wants to set up a commission of experts on how to deal with the result of the referendum.
But if the situation does not relax, Geywitz did not rule out talks with the FDP in the traffic light coalition about further tightenings in tenancy law.
The coalition agreement envisages a rent brake until 2029, a limitation of rent increases in tense housing markets and the expansion of the rental mirror.
I'm going to talk to the Minister of Justice to implement that as soon as possible.
If the rental market still does not relax, "we will talk to the coalition partners about further steps," emphasized the SPD politician.
