I'm annoyed by Sky Sport F1
Hello dear F1 fans, over the season the quality has decreased more and more on the German Sky, so I want to breathe a little with this post.
First of all, in the middle of the F2 race today, the transmission was canceled in order to start F1 pre-reporting on time.
Although due to the delayed start and the starting accident, the schedule was far behind the planning, but you could still have shown the last (planned) ten minutes as well as the championship decision (!).
It seems, however, that for legal reasons the F1 enjoys priority and therefore has to restrict everything else, so Sky DE probably had no choice here.
Stupid though, especially since Sky UK ended the race.
Nevertheless, a little praise: the commentator Olivier Zwartyes accompanied the difficult situation around the serious accident well.
Then in the F1 there was once again a lack of regular knowledge among the commentators Sascha Roos and Ralf Schumacher, so both did not know that under a red flag you can change tires.
Although this situation already existed in Imola, Baku and Silverstone this year, both only decided that Verstappen would be allowed to change tires when there were corresponding radio sayings on this topic to Hamilton.
At Sky UK as well as RTL, both commentators immediately knew that there is this possibility for Verstappen.
I am of the opinion that such elementary rules should simply be known when commenting on the F1 at a pay-TV station.
It's also not the first guesswork of what's now possible or mandated according to the rules, both simply have constant uncertainties on the subject of rules.
In general, it doesn’t please with Roos’ contrived commentation style, but that it’s a matter of taste.
But I seriously even like Heiko Wasser from RTL better.
In addition, there are constant sillinesses, both of which seem simply unprofessional, such as ordering coffee at (equally unsuspecting) reporter Peter Hardenacke or "UuuuuHD" by Ralf Schumacher.
The latter in particule brings a lot of unrest into the comment, which he apparently does not take it seriously.
Last but not least, the advertising simply takes over by Sky, in the run-out lap Sky is the only channel that goes into advertising, as you can listen to F1TV since only the German sound track has to manage without comment immediately after the race.
Neither ServusTV nor ORF do.
Also, these two broadcasters do less advertising in the trainings than Sky, and that as free TV stations.
Although you have to praise Glock and Baumgartner for their work, this alone does not make me overlook the disadvantages.
Sky Sport F1's rest programme is also very tenuous and full of repetitions.
Overall, Sky is really the worstest German-language broadcaster to broadcast the F1.
Unironically, RTL does a better job at the four races, which they are still allowed to broadcast, with the exception of advertising.
In any case, the terrific F1 season is much less fun than would be possible with a reasonable broadcaster.
I'd be interested in your opinion.
