The installation is very simple.
The fan pump is connected 4/6 mm to an outflower or similar by means of an air hose... and it can start.
The fan pump should be the same, or higher as the water level and should be mounted on the outside.
If the fan pump sits lower like the water level, you should put a check valve in between.
Easily cut through the air hose and put the valve in between.
This would prevent once water running backwards that the water runs out of the basin through the pump...
If the fan pump is installed outdoors, you, like other air pumps, you should be covered and protected from moisture
The pumps of the MK series are pure powerhouses that consume little energy
