Extra stress before holidays & holiday weekends
This topic came up with me last week.
But now I had to use my long weekend to relax.
That's why it's only now a post.
Not only before big holidays, such as the Christmas holidays, there is great stress in our company.
As it seems, it's also before holidays plus bridge days.
It was like this: Last week it was Ascension Day, which is called "Ascension" with us in Switzerland.
On Friday, the vast majority of people and companies do a bridge day, which is therefore semi-official.
So last week there was a long 4-day weekend in the house.
So what went on last week?
Stress Everywhere.
Loud e-mails, which absolutely had to come out even before the driveway, order here order there, everything *necessarily* before the long weekend.
Because... yes because?
Because "next week then" sounds like so much time and that mustn't be?
Or because, in a shortened week, do people want to do as much as in a normal week?
Not only was I stressed on Wednesday, but also mightily annoyed.
What's supposed to be self-hostilitation because of holidays?
Why do we still have holidays if we can’t treat ourselves properly?!
The stress didn't come from above, the colleagues were all so independent.
My question is simple: Aren't we, the Swiss?
Is this our reformed-evangelic kind?
Or do you know that in the north too?
