Fertility treatment at PKV / What is an "insurance case"?
hello together,
We were in fertility treatment for some time, now when it comes to billing with the PKV, it suddenly puts itself across.
In order:
We had applied for fertility training in advance at the PKV and received the promise of 3 attempts.
The experiments were not restricted in any way (e.g. time frame, success, etc.).
The first attempt led directly to the successful pregnancy and childbirth and was billed with PKV.
Some time later we tried to have a second child and carried out 2 (successful) attempts, but did not yet calculate them with the PKV.
We again applied for the assumption of costs at the PKV and were again granted 3 further attempts.
After a few more attempts (we carried out more attempts than agreed, logically calculate the most expensive with the PKV) we submitted the invoices to the PKV and got the nasty surprise: instead of 5 attempts (2+3), the PKV only wants to refund 3 attempts.
Justification: With pregnancy/birth, the remaining 2 attempts of the first commitment expire.
The second desire to have children is a new insurance claim.
According to the terms and conditions, however, "the insurance case begins with the healing treatment, it ends when there is no longer a need for treatment."
The questions to the experts in the round here:
* Who is right here, the PKV (only 3 attempts will be refunded) or we (there are 5 attempts to be refunded)?
* Should the PKV have told us in the pledges that with one birth the further trials will expire?
* Is the desire for a second child really a new insurance claim?
Infertility (due to closed fallopians) is not cured by the first child.
It would be great if the experts would give your opinion here.
Thank you so much for your help!
