Max Verstappen is said to have committed two rule breaks during the race, according to Mercedes.
Abu Dhabi - After Abu Dhabi's controversial Formula One finale, Mercedes has appealed.
The Silver Arrows suspect two rule breaks in the last Grand Prix of the year.
A protest refers to an alleged violation by Max Verstappen in the Red Bull in the last safety car phase, when he is said to have overtaken illegally.
A second objection was lodged against the evaluation at the end of the race.
According to Mercedes, the protocol was not followed in accordance with the rules.
Verstappen had overtaken Lewis Hamilton in the Mercedes on the last lap and had raced to his first Formula One title.
The manoeuvre took place shortly after the end of a safety car phase, in which the Dutchman had overtaken cars driving in front of him.
