Stages in the career of the new world champion Verstappen
The Dutcher Max Verstappen is the new world champion of Formula 1.
Ma Max Verstappen did it.
The Dutchman wins his first World Championship title in the Red Bull in his seventh year in Formula One.
His way to the summit of the premier class:
Abu Dhabi - 2012, Italy: Verstappen squanders the karting world championship after a crash in Sarno.
Father Jos Verstappen leaves him annoyed at a gas station on his way back.
His mother Sophie Kumpen picks up the teenager in the chariot.
2014, England: Red Bull's junior team gets auspicious offspring in Verstappen.
The 16-year-old follows in the footsteps of Sebastian Vettel and Daniel Ricciardo.
He continues for the time at European Formula 3.
2015, Australia: Verstappen enters a Grand Prix at the age of 17 years and 166 days as the youngest pilot in history.
Due to a defect, he has to turn off his Toro Rosso in Melbourne early.
2015, Malaysia: At 17 years and 180 days at the age of 17 and 180, Verstappen is also the youngest racer to score 1 points in Formula.
Verstappen finished seventh in Sepang at the Malaysian Grand Prix.
