We've had a new fiber optic connection in the house for a few weeks now.
Unfortunately, I am now having trouble setting up a stable Wi-Fi network.
Previously I had a DSL 50 Mbit connection and used Devolo DLan, which has received and sentered 50 Mbit except for a few failures.
The new fiber optic connection sends 500 Mbit to the FritzBox 7590 and to the DLan module, which is connected to the FritzBox, they also arrive.
However, on the other DLan module, which sends out the Wifi, no longer arrive the full 500, but the further I move away from the house with the module, the less arrives (i.e. use a socket that is located 1, 2, 3, etc. rooms away from the other module).
As a result, the Internet with the new fiber optic connection is now even slower on the first floor than before (\~45 Mbit).
I have also ordered a new Devolo Magic set, which apparently uses a new technology.
Although this was slightly better thafter than the DLan, there were similarly large losses here.
