When it's time to change your checking account
Who would have thought, now there would be rest in the current accounts, is deceived.
While many banks have used the autumn to be confirmed with all sorts of tricks from their customers the fee increases of the past, the allowances for negative interest rates continue to decline.
Deutsche Bank, for example, has long been considered relatively generous with a limit of 100,000 euros
Now she halved the allowance and even quartered for the daily allowance.
In a first step, the limit was lowered only for customers of the group division Postbank - to 50,000 euros for current and investment accounts and to 25,000 euros for daily cash accounts.
In the meantime, however, these lower allowances apply to the entire Deutsche Bank, as a spokesman confirmed on request.
And not only for new contracts, but also for "new individual agreements with existing customers".
Commerzbank had previously gone down to a limit of 50,000 euros, which still applies, as well as at ING Germany.
DKB, which is currently popular with cost-conscious customers, has lowered the allowances in two stages, initially to 50,000 euros, and now to 25,000 euros.
After all, more than 100 banks now have an allowance of 25,000 euros or less, according to figures frommated by the Internet portal Verivox.
Sparda-Bank Berlin has also arrived at 25,000 euros: However, there is still a legal dispute with the consumer centers, which in the first instance before the regional court Berlin against this regulation even got right.
It is now already being debated in the banks whether the institutions should possibly form provisions - in the event that the upper instances also declare the negative interest rates in principle inadmissible and many millions have to be repaid to bank customers.
