Kimi Räikkönen's farewell from Formula 1 was even quieter than expected.
Abu Dhabi - 42-year-old Finne took off his gloves and wiped sweat from his forehead.
That's it.
After a driving error and a slight gang touch, Räikkönen had to turn off his Alfa Romeo at the Abu Dhabi Grand Prix after not even half the race distance.
It was his 349th and last Grand Prix, the "Iceman" ending his career in motorsport's premier class.
As a farewell, his wife Minttu and the two children had also travelled to the United Arab Emirates.
Räikkönen's biggest success was to win the 2007 world championship in the Ferrari.
He managed 21 Grand Prix victories, started 18 times from the pole and came to the podium 103 times. dpa
