Laura Nolte won the women's third victory of the season in the bobsleigh.
After the previous day in monobob only for the fourth place, she raced to the World Cup victory on Sunday in the German triple success with pusher Deborah Levi.
Two-bobsleigh Olympic champion Mariama Jamanka from BRC Thuringia came in second place with Germany's fastest sprinter Alexandra Burghardt from Burghausen.
In addition to her Olympic qualifiers, she recorded the first podium place this winter.
Wiesbaden's Kim Kalicki finished third with Leonie Fiebig.
