Often on tour and still a lot of equipment?
There’s no problem with the Everyday V2 Backpack by Peak Design.
20 liters of capacity also swallow larger photo equipment without problems, which can be safely stowed with the help of the padded FlexFold dividers.
And what else you need in everyday objects, thanks to practical approaches in the individually configurable interior, remains well organized and separable from the photo equipment.
With the “update” of the Everyday Line to version 2 (V2), the series also presents itself in a new look.
The chic, minimalist design has a proverbially - with the Everyday Backpack series Peak Design has developed some highly innovative solutions that reliably protect the interior of the backpack, while still granting access to photo equipment in a matter of seconds.
This works with two options: Once conventionally via the lid flap, which can be closed with the MagLatch closure system, an excellently thought-out solution for effective protection, which has already proven itself with the messenger bags.
There is a closure hook made of metal with matching anchor beams on the front of the backpack in the closure flap.
In contrast than with most rucksacks, Peak Design has considered various “filling levels”: there are 4 anchor beams, stably riveted, into which the locking hook can be hooked.
If the backpack is fully loaded, you just take the top bar, it is rather empty, a deeper one.
Flap closure and hooks are also magnetic.
In this way, the backpack can also be reliably closed without locking the hook.
The second option also distinguishes the Everyday Backpack fundamentally from other, photo backpacks: In addition to the lid flap, there is also a zipper opening on both sides of the backpack.
This eliminates the biggest drawback of conventional backpacks with access from above - you don't have to dig through the contents anymore!
At the same time, this clever detail enormously increases the everyday suitability of the backpack: If you take not only your photo equipment, but also everyday objects or luggage.
In the Everyday Backpack, you can configure the interior individually (more about it below) and thus easily store both separately from each other - and access it independently through the two side openings.
So you can also pull the backpack in front of the body from the right side, for example, to access the camera equipment in the right main compartment, while the everyday things stay safely in the left half of the backpack and don't come in between.
Convenient, uncomplicatably adjustable carrying straps help with this.
And since the outer shell of the backpack is also made entirely of 100% recycled, weather-resistant nylon, the contents remain dry even if it is to go to Scotland in autumn.
