Coloma is the city where an unexpected event shaped the history of the West Coast.
In the winter of 1848, a man spotted glowing chunks in the water at the southern fork of the American River.
Although he tried to keep his discovery a secret, the news spread quickly, triggering the so-called “California Gold Rush” from ‘49.
Thousands came from near and far and made Coloma one of the country's fastest-growing and thriving cities.
Areas have been staked out, tents were pitched, and saloons and hotels were created almost overnight.
Everyone wanted their share of the country’s wealth.
For many it was: “Coloma or Bust” (Coloma or bankrupt)!
In this game you are a pioneer who seeks wealth in the West and wants to make a name.
You'll look for gold, recruit workers, gather horses and build businesses.
You’ll also have the opportunity to explore the surrounding rivers and adjacent areas.
You're not alone - the other pioneers seem to have the same idea!
You have to outperform your pioneer colleagues in order not to go bust with the rest of them.
Coloma is a quick strategy game with many ways to win.
You simultaneously choose your actions, have to budget with your resources and set up a tableau, which “works more and more” for you (so-called “Engine Building”).
The buildings on your tableau allow you to become more efficient, receive additional promotions, or turn rules in your favor.
With these buildings and the dynamic bridge tiles, you can develop your individual playing style with the help of fine adjustments.
Coloma plays over a three-year period from 1848 (the year in which the gold was discovered in Coloma), over 1849 (the year of the California Gold Rush) to 1850 (the year in whice California obtained official statehood).
One year in Coloma consists of five rounds.
During each round, the players will secretly and at the same time select a location on the schedule where they can perform actions.
After that, their selection is revealed and they place their pioneers on the appropriate locations.
If a location has the most pioneers, it gets a barrier!
This deactivates one half of the site - which reduces the possible actions there.
Then the players alternately carry out actions, such as winning resources, moving chariots, setting up tents, searching rivers, building bridges, opening shops, and positioning gunslingers.
When all actions are completed, the pioneers return.
At the beginning of each round, the advertiser turns to a new location and thus changes the available promotions.
This continues until the advertiser has moved five times, i.e
There's a shootout where players have to defend Coloma from a robbery of angry bandits.
If the players have contributed enough gunslingers and are numerically superior to the bandits, they receive rewards.
However, if they fail, they get fewer rewards or end in the cemetery.
The game ends after the third shooting, then there's the final evaluation.
The player with the most winning points wins!
