Holetschek: Countries advise on omissification of testing requirement for triple vaccinated
The health ministers of the countries want to decide at their next meeting on a nationwide omission of the testing requirement for triple vaccinated people.
"We countries quickly need clarity as to whether and from when for three times vaccinated the testing obligation can be omitted," Klaus Holetschek (CSU), chairman of the health ministers' conference, told Bild am Sonntag.
The omission of 2G plus for triple vaccinated is "not only medically meaningful, but also provides an additional vaccination incentive," Holetschek said.
Federal Health Minister Karl Lauterbach (SPD) has pledged "that he will make a proposal to the Conference of Ministers of Health next Tuesday". − afp
