Iran sees progress on nuclear deal negotiations
In the negotiations on a revival of the international nuclear agreement, progress is emerging, according to Iranian data.
"Both sides are on the verge of agreeing on the issues that are supposed to be on the agenda," Iran's chief negotiator Ali Bagheri told the Irna news agency on Sunday.
This is a "positive and important development", because initially there was not even agreement on the topics to be negotiated.
The deal is intended to prevent Iran from building nuclear weapons.
On Thursday, the Viennese talks on the revival of the agreement had been resumed after almost one-week interruption.
Negotiators from Iran, Germany, Britain, China, France and Russia take part in the negotiations.
A U.S. delegation is also on the ground in Vienna, but only indirectly involved in the negotiations.
Thuringia overtakes Saxony - Free State now state with highest corona incidence
Thuringia has replaced Saxony and currently has the highest incidence nationwide.
As the only federal state, the value is above the mark of 1000.
Thuringia was the only federal state at the Corona incidence on Sunday above the mark of 1000.
The Robert Koch Institute reported the seven-day value with 1025 new infections per 100,000 inhabitants.
In Saxony, which has always had the highest incidence nationwide, this figure stood at 990.5 on Sunday.
On Friday and Saturday, the incidence in Thuringia had fallen slightly, but had also been above the value of 1000.
In Thuringia, 2242 new contagions with the Sars-CoV-2 virus and 16 other deaths related to infection were reported within a day.
200 people suffering from Covid-19 were treated intensive care in hospitals on Sunday.
