Lahnsteiner Wehr equipped for water rescue: 45,000 euros subsidy from the land
Recently, the Rhineland-Palatinate Interior Minister Roger Lewentz handed over a donation notice of 45,000 euros for the new equipment truck water rescue of the volunteer fire brigade Lahnstein to Lord Mayor Peter Labonte.
The total cost of the vehicle, which has been in use since November 2020, amounted to 135,000 euros.
A good and important investment in security.
I am pleased that the state of Rhineland-Palatinate is supporting us here," says Lahnstein's Lord Mayor Peter Labonte.
The truck is used by Taucherstaffel Lahnstein, one of a total of seven units in Rhineland-Palatinate.
Above and under water, they perform tasks in water and ice rescue as well as technical assistance.
In Lahnstein, one constantly expects increasing deployments: The boom of hotel shipping on the Rhine and Moselle as well as the further increasing use of the Lahn as a leisure river contribute to this.
