"Party we wanted to throw": Frankfurt celebrate after goal-rich comeback against Leverkusen
What a spectacular reaction from Eintracht Frankfurt.
After 22 minutes, Hesse, who were unsuccessful twice in series, were supposedly on their way to the next Bundesliga bust.
But then the SGE turned up, shot the frustracy about a mixed start to the season within a good hour and won furiously with 5:2. "It's madness what the boys have done today," coach Oliver Glasner cheered at DAZN and pronounced a "lump rate praise, to every individual who was involved".
Initially it looked like a renewed dampener for Frankfurt, who are now in ninth place still behind their expectations.
Patrik Schick had put the Leverkusen in the lead with 2:0.
What happened next also impressed the SGE coach.
"How the players came back then and put in a fantastic performance," Glasner continued.
I'm insanely happy with the performance we've shown and, of course, with the result.
Defender Christopher Lenz, who was able to get back on the pitch for the first time since the fourth matchday and his overcome muscle injury, also emphasized the morale of his team-mates.
"I believe our mentality is unbelievably great," the 27-year-old said and was delighted with a look at the result, especially for the spectators.
That was the party we wanted to throw today.
For the upcoming tasks, however, Glasner now wants to keep the focus with him, but sees himself well positioned with regard to the personnel situation.
It's extraordinary that we've all the players fit in December that all players are physically in a top constitution.
It's top work in our medical department, but also the players live highly professionally.
"Now we want to continue step by step and remain modest" and "go through the tasks until the turn of the year at this level".
Next is an away match at Borussia Mönchengladbach (18.30, Sky) on Wednesday in the course of the English week.
