The title pretends, I work as a vaccinator in mobile vaccination teams, in which (so far only) the BioNTech/Pfizer vaccine is mainly inoculated in nursing homes.
Since these are soon finished to a large extent, it goes on partly in vaccination centers for me afterwards.
I am happy to answer questions without time limit on the organizational and human aspects and also medical questions, if these are not related to one personally (e.g. "I take drug X, is compatible with the vaccination...").
In my area of responsibility is the education for the vaccination, the indication (person is entitled to a vaccination according to corona vaccination ordinance and no reasons that speak against it), the medical documentation and, if necessary, the emergency care for allergic reactions (never happened to me).
Vaccination itself is delegable to qualified personnel, e.g. medical professionals.
In vaccination teams, however, we often don't have one, but "only" (for God's sake not a lack of appreciation!) pharmaceutical-technical assistants for vaccine preparation, but who can't carry out vaccinations, so that I also carry out most of the vaccinations myself there.
Difficult "Huidler" question: Amberger knows the solution
What is a "Huidlerer"?
With this dialect word, sent in by an Amberger, has been provided in the BR television show "Wir in Bayern" for fierce reflection.
But unlike on many previous days, the term "Host mi?" this time remained unterrated by the callers.
No, it wasn't a "human who's nervous."
And also no one "to whom everything has to go quickly."
That's what people heard from the TV host, was completely wrong.
To which the man from Amberg announced the solution and thus probably also caused astonishment among many Upper Palatinates.
"The Huidler," viewers learned, "is a rag with which someone wipes out the oven."
Dialector Antony Rowley, interviewed by Bavarian television for years as an expert, confirmed this.
With the note that this is a typical Oberpfälzisch term, somehow derived from the rather well-known dialect word "Houdern".
With which an education gap was closed - probably also among some who have been living in the Amberg area for a long time.
